    {
      "id": "coordination-structures",
      "label": {
        "en": "Coordination structures as resource-scheduling architectures",
        "zh": "作为资源调度架构的协调结构"
      },
      "description": {
        "en": "Polity, firm, market, commons, and protocol as five instances of one object: an architecture for scheduling scarce resources under distributed, private information. Descriptive throughout: it ranks nothing, names no culprits, recommends nothing. Contains the Hayek/Scott information constraint, transaction-cost boundaries, Ostrom's commons, the protocol's three documented failure modes, and three falsifiers. Its use of credit-transport language is marked explicitly as a structural rhyme, not a derivation.",
        "zh": "政体、企业、市场、共同体、协议,是同一个对象的五个实例:在分布式私有信息下调度稀缺资源的架构。全篇描述性:不排名、不点名、不建议。含 Hayek/Scott 信息约束、交易成本边界、Ostrom 的共同体、协议的三种已知失效模式,以及三条 falsifier。它对 credit-transport 语言的使用被显式标注为结构性押韵,而不是推导。"
      },
      "url": "https://machengshen.github.io/theory/coordination-structures.md",
      "format": "text/markdown",
      "inLanguage": "en",
      "cognitiveState": "speculative",
      "confidence": 0.45,
